{"name":"Quince","hex":"#d4cb60","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Quince","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Quince"}],"entries":[{"title":"Quince","blocks":[{"text":"The quince is the sole member of the genus Cydonia in the Malinae subtribe of the Rosaceae family. It is a deciduous tree that bears hard, aromatic bright golden-yellow pome fruit, similar in appearance to a pear. Ripe quince fruits are hard, tart, and astringent. They are eaten raw or processed into jam, quince cheese, or alcoholic drinks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Pancrace_Bessa00.jpg/330px-Pancrace_Bessa00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quince"},{"title":"Quince (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Quince is an American e-commerce company that offers apparel, accessories, jewelry, home goods, wellness and beauty products. It is headquartered in San Francisco, California and markets a “manufacturer-to-consumer” (M2C) model, in which goods are produced by partner factories and shipped directly to customers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bf/Quince_Company_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quince_(company)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/A_quince_flower_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-A_quince_flower_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/A_quince_flower_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-A_quince_flower_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/A_quince_flower_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-A_quince_flower_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm